-- title:
--   The query core of Theorem 30 for arbitrary input arrays returns the value of the query
-- statement:
--   If the query core procedure meets its specification (`QueryCoreSpecP lim P`), $t\le m$, `Lim30 lim p t b0 U` holds, $A_L,A_R$ are bounded by $U$, the memory holds `DSReadyA p t aX aY b0 AL AR`, and the depth leaves room for two calls, then for $I,J<N$ the statement `queryAtCore`, run in the frame of the locals of queryAt with a result cell $r$, ends within `tQueryCore p.L p.m t + 60` steps with the value `queryValue p.m t (encRowA AL (I / (K0 N0))) (encColA AR (J / (K0 N0))) (outStrOfPos (stdLayout hmL) I J)` in the first local (the query of Lemma 28 for the encodings of the bands of $I$ and $J$), changing only the scratch areas (`SameOutside2`).
